---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import ToolPage from "@bt/ui/ToolPage.astro";
import AdSlot from "@bt/ui/AdSlot.astro";
import HijriConverter from "../../components/HijriConverter.tsx";
---
<Layout
  bleed
  lang="en"
  title="Hijri to Gregorian date converter (and back) | Baitaan"
  description="Convert any date from Gregorian to Hijri or from Hijri to Gregorian using the Umm al-Qura calendar. Free, no sign-up."
>
  <ToolPage
    heading="Hijri and Gregorian date converter"
    lead="Pick a direction and enter a date to get the matching date and the day of the week instantly, using the Umm al-Qura calendar."
    updated="Updated: November 2026"
    sourcesHeading="Sources"
    sources={[{ href: "https://www.ummulqura.org.sa/", label: "Umm al-Qura calendar" }]}
  >
    <HijriConverter client:load lang="en" />

    <Fragment slot="guide">
      <h2>What is the Umm al-Qura calendar?</h2>
      <p>Umm al-Qura is Saudi Arabia's official Hijri calendar. It is calculated in advance from astronomical data, so the start of a month can differ by one day in countries that rely on sighting the new moon.</p>

      <h2>Why does the length of a Hijri month vary?</h2>
      <p>A Hijri month has 29 or 30 days, and a Hijri year has about 354 days, roughly 11 days shorter than a Gregorian year.</p>

      <AdSlot unit="0000000000" label="Advertisement" />

      <h2>Examples on the Umm al-Qura calendar</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>1 Muharram 1447 AH = 26 June 2025</li>
        <li>1 Ramadan 1447 AH = 18 February 2026</li>
        <li>1 Shawwal 1447 AH (Eid al-Fitr) = 20 March 2026</li>
        <li>1 Muharram 1448 AH = 16 June 2026</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>A quick estimate without the converter</h2>
      <p>Gregorian year ≈ Hijri year − (Hijri year ÷ 33) + 622. For 1448: 1448 − 43.9 + 622 ≈ 2026, and 1448 AH did begin in June 2026. Use the converter for the exact day.</p>
      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <details class="bt-faq"><summary>What are the Hijri months?</summary><p>In order: Muharram, Safar, Rabi al-Awwal, Rabi al-Thani, Jumada al-Ula, Jumada al-Akhirah, Rajab, Shaban, Ramadan, Shawwal, Dhu al-Qadah and Dhu al-Hijjah.</p></details>
      <details class="bt-faq"><summary>Why does another site give a date one day off?</summary><p>Some sites use a fixed arithmetic Hijri calendar or local moon sighting instead of Umm al-Qura. This converter uses Umm al-Qura, Saudi Arabia's official calendar.</p></details>
      <details class="bt-faq"><summary>Does it work for dates of birth and documents?</summary><p>Yes. For an age in both calendars, use the <a class="text-link underline" href="/en/hisab-alumr-bilhijri/">Hijri age calculator</a>.</p></details>
    </Fragment>
  </ToolPage>
</Layout>
